      "explanation": "The new GlobalSearchView endpoint is only protected by IsAuthenticated (ensuring the user is logged in) but does not enforce any object‑level permission checks for the many model types it returns. The view directly returns objects filtered only by the request user’s global view permissions (e.g., request.user.has_perm("documents.view_document")) and then uses get_objects_for_user_owner_aware for object‑level filtering. However, for models like User, Group, MailRule, MailAccount, Workflow, and CustomField the code only checks a global view permission (e.g., "auth.view_user") and then queries the entire table without owner‑aware filtering, potentially exposing data to any authenticated user who has the global view permission. The policy states that global permissions grant view access, but object‑level permissions must still be respected (see docs/usage.md sections on object permissions). This missing per‑object authorization constitutes a Missing Authorization flaw.",
